A||||5||grinthock||Bad Idle - Backfire -Running Rich - Opinoins?||||1||
Z||000000||grinthock||08-19-2001||06:15 PM||||OK guys, after watching people get yelled at for not using the search -- I DID!  I did some checking.... Here is the situation.  Your OPINION is what I am looking for<P>Symptoms:<P>1)  When car is cold it runs REALLY BAD, backfire occasionally, hard shifts (auto) low power<P>2)  The car stumbles at low rpms, has a hard time getting going.<P>3)  The idles lopes to 800 sometimes 500 when IN gear at a light (the Torque Con Sol is already disconnected)<P>4)  I get exhaust detonation when it first starts sometimes, and sometimes after I turn it off I get detonation. <P>5)  The car is DRINKING FUEL!!  There is carbon on the exhaust tips (unburnt fuel?)<P><BR>Here is what I have done<P>1)  Confirmed IAC works fine<P>2)  NO CODES are coming from the ECM<P>3)  The ECM works, I disconnected the MAT to confirm that it WOULD kick a code.<P>4)  I drove it with the diagnostic connector shorted to see, and the car ran WORSE!! it wouldn't keep running at idle at ALL it just wanted to kill itself.  (I did this AFTER warm up of course)<P><BR>I am thinking TIMING here.... Any opinions?  I have NEVER receved codes from this car, you would think with it doing all this a code would fire.<P><BR>Thanks everyone||||reg||1
Z||000001||AkursedX||08-19-2001||06:48 PM||||I would say to check the timing as well.<BR>After I got my car back together, I adjusted the timing by hand until I got my hands on a light, and it ran great!  When I got the light, I found my timing was at 18 degrees, so I set it down to 10, and it ran crappy.  It would want to die when I 1st start it and would stumble until it warmed up.  So I bumped the timing up to 14 degrees and it runs good now.<BR>But I think it might be more than the timing if your are running terribly rich.  Maybe your O2 sensor is getting old and it might still be working, but might have carbon buildup which is interefering with a proper reading.  Also your plugs might be fouled or something else in the ignition system isn't up to par and you aren't getting enough spark to burn the fuel.  <BR>Hope this helps.<BR><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||08-19-2001||06:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AkursedX:<BR><B>I would say to check the timing as well.<BR>After I got my car back together, I adjusted the timing by hand until I got my hands on a light, and it ran great!  When I got the light, I found my timing was at 18 degrees, so I set it down to 10, and it ran crappy.  It would want to die when I 1st start it and would stumble until it warmed up.  So I bumped the timing up to 14 degrees and it runs good now.<BR>But I think it might be more than the timing if your are running terribly rich.  Maybe your O2 sensor is getting old and it might still be working, but might have carbon buildup which is interefering with a proper reading.  Also your plugs might be fouled or something else in the ignition system isn't up to par and you aren't getting enough spark to burn the fuel.  <BR>Hope this helps.<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Plugs are new, so that's not it, the O2 sensor I thought of UNTIL I put the car in diag mode (Which should IGNORE the O2 and use stock table values) and it got worse.||||reg||1
